Subject: [PATCH] dtl: propagate the DXCore class-layout definition to consumers

ImmediateContext contains m_DXCore only when DYNAMIC_LOAD_DXCORE is enabled.
Keeping the definition PRIVATE compiles consumers such as D3D11On12 against
an ImmediateContext with a different size and member offsets. Its inline
GetViewAllocator then addresses unrelated memory and hangs taking the wrong
mutex during render-target-view creation. Publish the definition with the
library so all translation units agree on the class ABI.

diff --git a/src/CMakeLists.txt b/src/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -100,7 +100,7 @@
 
 target_link_libraries(d3d12translationlayer Microsoft::DirectX-Headers d3d12 dxgi)
 
-target_compile_definitions(d3d12translationlayer PRIVATE DYNAMIC_LOAD_DXCORE=1)
+target_compile_definitions(d3d12translationlayer PUBLIC DYNAMIC_LOAD_DXCORE=1)
 target_compile_definitions(d3d12translationlayer PRIVATE TRANSLATION_LAYER_SUPPORTS_D3DKMT_PRESENT=1)
 
 if(USE_PIX)
